# Git: local-root vs main (do not confuse)

## This workspace is NEVER `main`

- Folder `d:\GHL_Montfort` is **always branch `local-root`**.
- `local-root` exists only so developers can **clone the full layout** (app + `reference/` + docs + HTTrack). It is **not** GHL and **not** production.
- Stay on `local-root`. Do **not** checkout `main` here. Do **not** merge `local-root` into `main` or `main` into `local-root`. Do **not** force-push `main`.

## What goes to GitHub `main`

GHL fetches `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/FerozArshad/montfortre/main/<path>`.

Push **only** new/updated **React/Vite app files** under `ghl-react/`, with paths **rewritten to repo root**:

- `ghl-react/src/...` → `src/...`
- `ghl-react/public/...` → `public/...`
- `ghl-react/index.html` → `index.html`
- `ghl-react/package.json` → `package.json` (only if the app actually needed a package change)
- App docs GHL uses: `DOCUMENTATION.md`, `GHL-PASTE-TO-STUDIO.md`, `GHL-TRANSFER-TRACKING.md`, `seo-audit/...` when those files changed for the migration

Copy into a **separate** `main` worktree/clone, commit on `feature/<name>-ghl`, push, then **fast-forward** `git push origin HEAD:main`.

## Never push to `main`

- `reference/`
- `.cursor/`
- parent-tree files that only exist on `local-root`
- `ghl-react/package-lock.json` unless the user explicitly asks
- the whole `ghl-react/` folder prefix (GHL paths have **no** `ghl-react/` prefix)

## Workflow reminder

1. Implement on `local-root`.
2. Optionally commit/push `origin local-root` so the clone layout is backed up.
3. Ship GHL by copying **rewritten** app files onto `main` — not by merging branches.
